# Trivy Ignore File
# CVE IDs listed here (one per line) will be excluded from security scans
#
# Use this for:
# - Known false positives
# - Vulnerabilities accepted as acceptable risk
# - Issues being tracked elsewhere
#
# NOTE: ignore-unfixed=true in workflow already filters unfixable vulnerabilities
# Only add CVEs here if they require explicit exclusion
#
# Example format:
# CVE-2024-12345
# CVE-2024-67890

# Add specific CVE exclusions below this line

# scikit-learn 0.23.2 in env_nanosim only (#175). NanoSim's pretrained KDE
# pickles load only on sklearn 0.23 (sklearn.neighbors._dist_metrics), so it
# cannot be upgraded. Neither CVE is reachable: NanoSim only loads and samples
# KernelDensity models; it never uses SVM or text vectorizers. Re-check on
# expiry or when NanoSim ships models for a newer scikit-learn.
# CVE-2020-28975: sklearn.svm libsvm crafted-model crash (disputed upstream).
CVE-2020-28975 exp:2027-05-09
# CVE-2024-5206: TfidfVectorizer stop_words_ keeps leaked tokens.
CVE-2024-5206 exp:2027-05-09
